</svg></div></a><div class="hide w-embed"><p fs-copyclip-element="copy-this">https://www.aikido.dev/blog/two-malicious-agent-framework-releases-hit-pypi-in-33-minutes</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></div><div><section class="section-component"><div data-wf--section-spacing-padding--variant="large-7rem---default" class="section-spacer"></div><div class="container"><div data-wf--re-row--variant="top-left" class="row-component"><div class="row"><div data-wf--re-column--variant="fill" class="col"><div class="slot cc-column"><h2 STYLE="font-size:1.5rem" class="heading-component"><span>Recently Added</span></h2></div></div></div></div><div data-wf--spacer--variant="2-rem" class="spacer w-variant-90fe0d3b-db40-7355-2541-54928cd9b516"></div><div data-wf--re-row--variant="top-left" class="row-component"><div class="row"><div data-wf--re-column--variant="fill" class="col"><div class="slot cc-column"><div class="blog-posts-wrapper w-dyn-list"><div fs-list-element="list" role="list" class="blog-posts_list w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="blog-posts_item w-dyn-item"><div class="blog-posts_post"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/642adcaf364024654c71df23/6afc522ba13a27d8917e0a59_Group%202147256808.png" loading="lazy" alt="" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/642adcaf364024654c71df23/6afc522ba13a27d8917e0a59_Group%202147256808-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/642adcaf364024654c71df23/6afc522ba13a27d8917e0a59_Group%202147256808-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/642adcaf364024654c71df23/6afc522ba13a27d8917e0a59_Group%202147256808-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/642adcaf364024654c71df23/6afc522ba13a27d8917e0a59_Group%202147256808-p-1600.png 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/642adcaf364024654c71df23/6afc522ba13a27d8917e0a59_Group%202147256808.png 1920w" class="blog-post_img"/><div class="blog-post_content"><div data-wf--re-plain-text--variant="14px" STYLE="margin-bottom:0.5rem; text-transform: uppercase;" class="plain-text-component w-variant-21c22b07-aa00-a1e3-f6d3-2bcb1c711373"><div data-wf--re-plain-text-color--variant="neutral-500" class="plain-text-color w-variant-960a0f75-2e42-d9be-f97a-bf0a0dd5f949"><div>November 17, 2026</div></div></div><h3 STYLE="margin-bottom:1rem; font-size:1.5rem" class="heading-component"><span>Java4Shell: RCE flaw in OpenJDK&#x27;s Base64 decoder, with affected versions and fix (CVE-2026-114938)</span></h3><div data-wf--re-plain-text--variant="16px" STYLE="margin-bottom:1rem" class="plain-text-component text-style-3lines"><div data-wf--re-plain-text-color--variant="base-color" class="plain-text-color"><div>Java4Shell is a flaw in OpenJDK’s Base64 decoder that can let attackers run code remotely, sometimes without authentication. Here are the affected versions, the fixed builds and how to mitigate it today.</div></div></div><a data-wf--button-tertiary-new--variant="black" data-wf-native-id-path="013ade1e-2f66-78a8-ea72-e1e789a143fc_instance-0:b4b634b4-45ff-aec7-0b7a-5e6645a1fbad_instance-0" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="b4b634b4-45ff-aec7-0b7a-5e6645a1fbad" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265f2e16478f0b82120e5cccb%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%226afc5251f2a66d5f9bd3a309%22%7D%5D" data-wf-component-context="%5B%7B%22componentId%22%3A%22b4b634b4-45ff-aec7-0b7a-5e6645a1fbad%22%2C%22instanceId%22%3A%22013ade1e-2f66-78a8-ea72-e1e789a143fc%22%7D%5D" href="/blog/java-17-rce-vulnerability-cve-2026-114938" class="u-button-tretiary w-variant-153e1cf3-d221-a28e-167e-67f75ea6502d w-inline-block"><div class="button_tretiary_text w-variant-153e1cf3-d221-a28e-167e-67f75ea6502d">Read more</div><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" viewBox="0 0 21 20" fill="none" class="button_tretiary_arrow w-variant-153e1cf3-d221-a28e-167e-67f75ea6502d"><path d="M15.9417 9.55833C16.0581 9.67584 16.1234 9.83457 16.1234 10C16.1234 10.1654 16.0581 1